You bravely walk to the shrubs of lilac plants, and when you touch branches to move them apart, you feel something humid and sticky on your hand! The branch is entirely covered in fuzz with glittering drops of limpid liquid. You move sharply with your hand to release it, but it's useless, fuzz is tenaciously holding it. Other branches are predatory tremble near. Almost like alive. You feel yourself a fly, trapped in a web. You need to pull yourself together and find the way out. 